The instability ultimately involved three separate problems:

Two OpenClaw CLI installations existed simultaneously, 
with an older user-local CLI being invoked against state created by a newer system-wide installation.
OpenClaw 2026.7.2-beta.6 was published without corresponding beta.6 releases of several official plugins, 
making exact version alignment impossible.
After upgrading everything to 2026.7.2-beta.7, a locally installed WhatsApp health-check watchdog still 
referenced the removed old CLI path. 

Its failed health checks repeatedly restarted the otherwise healthy Gateway.

The final issue was particularly misleading because Gateway probes frequently returned ECONNREFUSED or 
WebSocket 1006, even though the Gateway was functioning correctly between watchdog-triggered restarts.

