Issue 1 — Multiple OpenClaw CLI Installations
Symptoms

The system initially had two different OpenClaw installations.

An older user-local npm installation was being executed:

~/.npm-global/bin/openclaw
2026.7.1-2

while the system service was using the newer installation:

/usr/bin/openclaw
2026.7.2-beta.6

This caused the older CLI to attempt to access state created by the newer release.

A representative error was:

OpenClaw state database ~/.openclaw/state/openclaw.sqlite
uses newer schema version 6;
this OpenClaw build supports 1.
Root Cause

Shell PATH resolution was still selecting the old user npm installation.

The Gateway itself was running from the newer system installation.

Effectively:

CLI
  ↓
old OpenClaw

Gateway
  ↓
new OpenClaw

State DB
  ↓
new schema

This caused misleading schema and configuration errors.

Resolution

Remove the obsolete user-global installation:

npm uninstall -g openclaw
hash -r

Then verify:

openclaw --version
type -a openclaw

The expected CLI should be:

/usr/bin/openclaw

The CLI and Gateway should report the same version.

